"}},{"titleInfo":{"title":"Nickel and dimed","subTitle":"on (not) getting by in America"},"name":{"@nameTitleGroup":"1","@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Ehrenreich, Barbara","role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}}},"typeOfResource":"text","originInfo":{"place":[{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"nyu"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"New York (State)"}]},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York"}}],"publisher":"Henry Holt & Co.","dateIssued":["c2008",{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"2008"}],"issuance":"monographic"},"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"244 p. ; 21 cm."},"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"Nickel and Dimed is a modern classic that deftly portrays the plight of America's working-class poor. Author Barbara Ehrenreich decides to see if she can scratch out a comfortable living in blue-collar America. What she discovers is a culture of desperation, where workers often take multiple low-paying jobs just to keep a roof overhead."},"tableOfContents":"Introduction: Getting ready -- Serving in Florida -- Scrubbing in Maine -- Selling in Minnesota -- Evaluation -- Reader's guide.","note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Barbara Ehrenreich."},"Originally published in hardcover in 2001 by Metropolitan Books ; first Holt Paperbacks edition, 2002.",{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references."}],"subject":[{"geographicCode":{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"n-us---"}},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Minimum wage","geographic":"United States"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Unskilled labor","geographic":"United States"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Poverty","geographic":"United States"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Working poor","geographic":"United States"}],"classification":{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"HD4918 .E375 2008"},"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9780805088380"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"0805088385"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"182737658"}],"relatedItem":{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990115111160203941/catalog"}},"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://id.loc.gov/rwo/agents/no2014094889","#text":"Widener Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"HD4918 .E375 2008"},null,null],"extension":[{"librarycloud":{"HarvardRepositories":{"HarvardRepository":"Widener"},"originalDocument":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/harvard.librarycloud.marc/990115111160203941","priorrecordids":{"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALEPH","#text":"011511116"}},"processingDate":"2023-10-30T05:22Z"}},{"sets":null}],"recordInfo":{"recordContentSource":{"@authority":"marcorg","#text":"BTCTA"},"recordCreationDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"071130"},"recordChangeDate":{"@encoding":"iso8601","#text":"20080725"},"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALMA","#text":"990115111160203941"},"recordOrigin":"Converted from MARCXML to MODS version 3.6 using MARC21slim2MODS3-6.xsl\n        (Revision 1.117 2017/02/14)"}},{"@version":"3.8","titleInfo":{"title":"Nickel and dimed ","subTitle":"on (not) getting by in America "},"name":{"@usage":"primary","@type":"personal","namePart":"Ehrenreich, Barbara","role":{"roleTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"creator"}}},"typeOfResource":"text","originInfo":{"place":[{"placeTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"nyu"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"marccountry","#text":"New York (State)"}]},{"placeTerm":{"@type":"text","#text":"New York "}}],"issuance":"monographic","agent":{"namePart":"Picador"},"dateIssued":"2011","edition":"1st Picador ed."},"language":{"languageTerm":[{"@type":"code","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"eng"},{"@type":"text","@authority":"iso639-2b","#text":"English"}]},"physicalDescription":{"form":{"@authority":"marcform","#text":"print"},"extent":"244 p. ; 21 cm."},"abstract":{"@type":"Summary","#text":"\"Millions of Americans work full-time, year-round, for poverty-level wages. In 1998, Barbara Ehrenreich decided to join them. She was inspired in part by the rhetoric surrounding welfare reform, which promised that a job--any job--can be the ticket to a better life. But how does anyone survive, let alone prosper, on $6 an hour? To find out, Ehrenreich left her home, took the cheapest lodgings she could find, and accepted whatever jobs she was offered. Moving from Florida to Maine to Minnesota, she worked as a waitress, a hotel maid, a cleaning woman, a nursing home aide, and a Wal-Mart sales clerk. She lived in trailer parks and crumbling residential motels. Very quickly, she discovered that no job is truly \"unskilled,\" that even the lowliest occupations require exhausting mental and muscular effort. She also learned that one job is not enough; you need at least two if you intend to live indoors. Nickel and Dimed reveals low-rent America in all its tenacity, anxiety, and surprising generosity--a land of Big Boxes, fast food, and a thousand desperate strategems for survival. Read it for the smoldering clarity of Ehrenreich's perspective and for a rare view of how \"prosperity\" looks from the bottom. You will never see anything--from a motel bathroom to a restaurant meal--quite the same way again. \"-- Provided by publisher."},"tableOfContents":{"@type":"Contents","#text":"Getting ready -- Serving in Florida -- Scrubbing in Maine -- Selling in Minnesota -- Evaluation -- Afterword : Nickel and dimed."},"note":[{"@type":"statement of responsibility","#text":"Barbara Ehrenreich."},"\"With a new afterword\"--Cover.",{"@type":"bibliography","#text":"Includes bibliographical references."}],"subject":[{"geographicCode":{"@authority":"marcgac","#text":"n-us---"}},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Minimum wage","geographic":"United States"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Working poor","geographic":"United States"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Unskilled labor","geographic":"United States"},{"@authority":"lcsh","topic":"Poverty","geographic":"United States"},{"@authority":"mesh","topic":"Salaries and Fringe Benefits","geographic":"United States"},{"@authority":"mesh","geographic":"United States"}],"classification":[{"@authority":"lcc","#text":"HD4918 .E375 2011"},{"@authority":"nlm","#text":"HD 4918 E33n 2011"},{"@edition":"22","@authority":"ddc","#text":"305.5/69092 B"}],"identifier":[{"@type":"isbn","#text":"9780312626686 (pbk.)"},{"@type":"isbn","#text":"0312626681 (pbk.)"},{"@type":"lccn","#text":"^^2011013114"},{"@type":"oclc","#text":"682894484"}],"relatedItem":{"@otherType":"HOLLIS record","location":{"url":"https://id.lib.harvard.edu/alma/990130785960203941/catalog"}},"location":[{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/0000000463633307","#text":"Lamont Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":"HD4918 .E375 2011"},{"physicalLocation":{"@displayLabel":"Harvard repository","@type":"repository","@valueURI":"http://isni.org/isni/000000011940971X","#text":"Harvard Law School Library, Harvard University"},"shelfLocator":" HD4918   .E375 2011 "},null,null],"extension":[{"librarycloud":{"HarvardRepositories":{"HarvardRepository":["Lamont","Law School"]},"originalDocument":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/harvard.librarycloud.marc/990130785960203941","priorrecordids":{"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALEPH","#text":"013078596"}},"processingDate":"2026-10-22T04:14Z"}},{"sets":null}],"recordInfo":{"descriptionStandard":"aacr","recordContentSource":{"@authority":"marcorg","#text":"DLC"},"recordCreationDate":{"@encoding":"marc","#text":"110404"},"recordChangeDate":{"@encoding":"iso8601","#text":"20120222"},"recordIdentifier":{"@source":"MH:ALMA","#text":"990130785960203941"},"recordOrigin":"Converted from MARCXML to MODS version 3